          "date": "2026-10-23 09:51:17.000000000",
          "tz": 480
        },
        "subject": "LU-20737 tests: freeze lwp LRU in sanity test_120f",
        "message": "LU-20737 tests: freeze lwp LRU in sanity test_120f\n\nsanity test_120f samples ldlm.services.ldlm_canceld.stats around\nmrename and expects no extra LDLM_CANCEL RPCs.  The test freezes\nclient mdc/osc LRU, but not the server-side lwp namespaces.\nUnused qsd per-ID quota locks in lwp can be reclaimed by the\nperiodic client LRU recalc and send standalone LDLM_CANCEL RPCs\nto ldlm_canceld, making can2-can1 non-zero and causing\n\"N cancel RPC occured.\"\n\nClear and freeze the lwp LRU before can1 by using a non-zero\nlru_size to disable LRU resize, and raise lru_max_age to 3900s\nas lru_resize_disable() does for mdc/osc.  Restore both lru_size\nand lru_max_age via stack_trap.\n\nSigned-off-by: Xiyang Wang <xiwang@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: I4cf5348417f206cec57a7cce5e65459e0197efb0\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
